## Recommended split between the two projects

The clean architecture is:

```text
                    URIEL ECOSYSTEM
                           │
             ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
             │                           │
        UrielSnips                  Uriel Studio
             │                           │
      Writing snippets             Full authoring IDE
             │                           │
      Templates/prompts            Project management
             │                     Manuscript
             │                     Characters
             │                     Codex
             │                     Timeline
             │                     Worldbuilding
             │                     AI
             │                     LSP
             │                     Export
             │                           │
             └───────────┬───────────────┘
                         │
                  Shared Uriel Core
                         │
              ┌──────────┼──────────┐
              │          │          │
           Entities    Language    Schemas
              │          │          │
              └──────────┼──────────┘
                         │
                       Parser
```

**The critical design decision:** `UrielSnips` should remain lightweight and independently installable, while **Uriel Studio becomes the full platform**. The shared data/schema layer should eventually prevent the two projects from developing incompatible definitions of characters, lore, scenes, AI blocks, and other Uriel concepts.
